WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.360
I was shocked to learn recently that some scientists want to scale back their research in an effort to decrease carbon emissions.
我最近得知，一些科学家为了减少碳排放，想要缩减自己的研究，这让我大为震惊。

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.850
The crisis is here, they said, and we need to cut back on our energy-intensive modelling.
他们说，危机已经到来，我们需要减少高耗能的建模工作。

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.030
At the very least, we need to make our energy use far more sustainable.
最起码，我们需要大幅提高自身能源使用的可持续性。

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:34.330
It is unarguable that our laboratories, scientific instruments, rockets and satellites—the tools we scientists need to measure the planet’s pulse—demand significant amounts of energy in both their construction and operation.
无可争辩的是，我们的实验室、科学仪器、火箭和卫星，也就是我们科学家测量地球脉搏所需的工具，无论建造还是运行，都需要消耗大量能源。

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:44.070
And it is equally true that science’s unrelenting appetite for information has caused a mushrooming of energy-intensive data centres around the world.
而且同样属实的是，科学对信息永无止境的渴求，已导致高耗能的数据中心在世界各地如雨后春笋般涌现。

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:51.990
According to the International Energy Agency, these buildings now consume about 1 percent of the world’s electricity.
据国际能源署称，这些建筑如今消耗着全世界约1%的电力。

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.300
However, this is a price we must pay for understanding the world.
然而，这是我们为认识世界而必须付出的代价。

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:08.870
How can we inform decision makers about the best ways to bring down carbon emissions if we can’t track the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere, where it’s coming from and who’s producing it?
如果我们无法追踪大气中二氧化碳的含量，以及它从哪里来、是谁排放的，又怎能告诉决策者减少碳排放的最佳途径呢？

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:17.050
The carbon emissions from technological research are well spent: ultimately this research will safeguard the future of our planet.
技术研究产生的碳排放是物有所值的：这类研究最终将守护我们这个星球的未来。

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:29.260
It can be hard for scientists to make the case because our work is complex, often takes place behind closed doors and does not always lend itself to easy interpretation or explanation.
科学家可能很难把这个道理讲清楚，因为我们的工作很复杂，往往关起门来进行，而且并不总是易于解读或解释。

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.310
But demonstrating the efficacy of science will be crucial if we are to solve humanity’s greatest challenges.
但如果我们要解决人类面临的最大挑战，证明科学的功效将至关重要。

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:43.450
It is all too easy to feel paralysed in the face of daunting problems such as climate change and to do nothing.
面对气候变化这类令人生畏的难题，人们实在太容易感到不知所措，什么也不做。

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:54.950
But then I think of a friend’s daughter who turned her fears into action: she became a wind energy engineer and now thrives on delivering renewable energy, limiting emissions.
但这时我就会想起一位朋友的女儿，她把恐惧化作了行动：她成了一名风能工程师，如今在提供可再生能源、限制排放的工作中如鱼得水。

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:08.490
Recognising the hope that science and engineering can bring was the impetus behind the creation of the Millennium Technology Prize, which is now entering its 20th year as a celebration of human ingenuity.
认识到科学与工程能够带来希望，正是设立千禧技术奖的动力所在；这一礼赞人类创造才能的奖项，如今正迈入第20个年头。

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:22.860
One of the past winners, Professor Martin Green from the University of New South Wales, Australia, is the inventor of the Passivated Emitter and Rear Cell technology, which is now found in most of the world’s solar panels.
往届得主之一、澳大利亚新南威尔士大学的马丁·格林教授，是钝化发射极和背面电池技术的发明者，如今世界上大多数太阳能电池板都采用了这项技术。

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.700
Thanks to his invention, we have a real chance to decrease the world’s carbon emissions.
多亏了他的这项发明，我们才真正有机会减少全世界的碳排放。

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:42.440
Every day, scientists, technologists and engineers are discovering new ways to exploit renewable energy sources and develop techniques not just to use power more intelligently but to power our intelligence.
科学家、技术专家和工程师每天都在发现新的方法，以开发利用可再生能源，并研发各种技术，这些技术不仅能让我们更智能地使用电力，还能为我们的智能提供动力。

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:50.770
A great example of this is Europe’s largest supercomputer, LUMI in Finland, which is astonishingly carbon-negative.
欧洲最大的超级计算机、位于芬兰的LUMI就是这方面的一个绝佳例子，令人惊讶的是，它实现了负碳排放。

00:02:51.570 --> 00:03:00.170
Established in an old paper mill, it is powered by a nearby river, and its waste heat warms the people who live in the surrounding town of Kajaani.
它设在一座旧造纸厂里，由附近的一条河流供电，产生的余热则为周边卡亚尼镇的居民供暖。

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:09.610
If the world is to meet its net-zero ambitions, we must think hard about how we can deliver sustainable computing and deliver more LUMIs.
如果世界要实现净零目标，我们就必须认真思考，如何才能实现可持续计算、打造更多像LUMI这样的超级计算机。
